  "title": "sync/async - tastytrade 11.1.0 documentation",
  "content": "After creating a session (which is always initialized synchronously), the rest of the API endpoints implemented in the SDK have both sync and async implementations as of version 9.0.\n\nLet’s see how this looks:\n\nThe async implementation is similar:\n\nThat’s it! All sync methods have a parallel async method that starts with a_.\n\nPlease note that two modules, tastytrade.backtest and tastytrade.streamer, only have async implementations. But for everything else, you can use what you’d like!",
  "headings": [
    {
      "level": "h1",
      "text": "sync/async¶",
      "id": "sync-async"
    }
  ],
  "code_samples": [
    {
      "code": "from tastytrade Account, Session\nsession = Session(username, password)\n# using sync implementation\naccounts = Account.get(session)",
      "language": "julia"
    },
    {
      "code": "from tastytrade Account, Session\nsession = Session(username, password)\n# using async implementation\naccounts = await Account.a_get(session)",
      "language": "julia"
    }
  ],
